APPLICATION CHECKLIST

1. Check hardware, receiver capabilities, vendor offload components, source
   revisions, licenses and backups; stop any build using the target tree.
2. Run git apply --check, then git apply in each specified target repository;
   patch paths are relative to that repository, not the Android root.
3. Review the resulting source changes and build through the ROM's normal
   device-specific workflow. Do not mix different patch editions.
4. Validate negotiated codec/rate, controller acknowledgements, audible output,
   gaming-mode transitions and reconnect behavior on the actual device.
